WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.135
-The Democrats won back control

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:04.170
of the House of Representatives
tonight

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.605
for the first time
in eight years,

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.573
putting President Trump's
agenda...

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.742
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:12.545
Yeah, it happened.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.680
...putting President Trump's
agenda in serious danger.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.916
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:21.187
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.623
Well, cable news
was unanimous --

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.525
it was a blue wave.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.426
-When you look
at what's going on here tonight,

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:29.462
this is not a blue wave.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:30.963
-So, we haven't seen
the blue wave.

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:32.598
-There is not
a blue wave forming.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:33.699
-It's not a blue wave.

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:34.967
-This is not a blue wave.

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:36.269
-It is not a blue wave.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.938
-So, cable news wasn't sure
if it was a blue wave,

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.007
but we here at "Late Night"
can confidently say

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.510
that it was at least
a blue ripple.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.478
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.780
-Blue ripple!

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.883
-But, hey.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.151
If you've been
in the desert for two years,

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:55.354
a little splash of water
feels like a damn tsunami.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:56.623
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:59.592
So, come on, Democrats,
give me some good news,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:03.096
or I'm gonna have to drink
this entire bottle of whiskey.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.264
-NBC News is predicting

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:09.068
the Democrats will control
the House of Representatives.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.170
-Yeah, I did it, anyway!

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.005
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.441
Because that's
the thing about alcohol --

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:18.478
it works for good or bad news.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.679
That's right, the Democrats
are projected to take control

00:01:20.679 --> 00:01:22.715
of the House for the first time
in eight years

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.050
even though they
lost seats in the Senate,

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.954
and that's because the House and
Senate maps were very different,

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.589
as CBS explained.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:33.025
-It looks like we have races
on two planets.

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:36.295
We have Planet Senate
and we have Planet House.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:38.531
-That's right, the Senate
is a different planet,

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.800
which explains why Ted Cruz

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.835
looks like he burst
out of someone's chest.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:43.936
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.936 --> 00:01:46.505
Now, tonight was a crazy,
frenetic night,

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:47.906
with results
that were all over the map.

00:01:47.906 --> 00:01:51.344
In fact, things were so crazy,
MSNBC's Steve Kornacki

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:55.314
was wearing three different
mic packs all at once.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:57.750
I knew Steve Kornacki was busy,
but I didn't know

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.186
he was on three different
networks at the same time.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.488
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:03.089
So, the results
were all over the place.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.058
Just to give you an idea of
how crazy things were tonight,

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:07.460
Beto O'Rourke
lost to Ted Cruz in Texas

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.330
while Republican Kris Kobach
lost to a Democrat in Kansas.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.799
Democratic Senator
Heidi Heitkamp,

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:15.935
she lost in North Dakota,
while in Colorado,

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:19.272
we saw the nation's first openly
gay man to be elected governor.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:23.543
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:26.579
In a huge victory, Kim Davis,
the Kentucky clerk

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:29.282
who infamously refused
to issue marriage licenses

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:32.017
to same-sex couples,
lost her re-election bid.

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:35.421
And fun fact -- her opponent
was a gay wedding cake.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.957
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.226
Now, here's the thing --
Democrats winning back

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.594
control of the House
is a huge development

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.762
for a number of reasons.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:45.231
It'll stop Republicans
from repealing Obamacare

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.565
and drastically cutting programs

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.067
like Social Security
and Medicare.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.236
It will also allow Democrats to
protect the Russia investigation

00:02:51.236 --> 00:02:53.906
and will put Democrats
in charge of House Committees,

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:56.342
which gives them
a huge new power.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.144
-If Democrats do take the House,

00:02:58.144 --> 00:03:00.012
President Trump will wake up
Wednesday morning

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:02.448
to a very different
political scenario.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.116
Here on the Hill,
they are going to

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:06.952
investigate this President and
his administration thoroughly,

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:08.921
putting it under
an intense microscope,

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:11.757
likely investigating everything
from the President's tax returns

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:12.892
to conflict of interest

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.127
to those questions
about Russian collusion.

00:03:15.127 --> 00:03:17.964
-Even when a party
has only one house of Congress,

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.665
that can still
have a really big impact,

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:22.634
because once they're controlling
that house of Congress,

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:25.371
they get to conduct oversight
of the administration.

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.673
They have subpoena power
to help them do that.

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:30.376
-That's right -- Democrats
now have subpoena power,

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.045
and if you don't believe me,
Trump was just photographed

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.881
trying to sneak 20 years
of tax returns

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.049
out of the White House.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.450
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.653
Right now, Trump is at an
OfficeMax in Washington, D.C. --

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.121
"Yes. Do you have a shredder?

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.156
No, I, uh --
I just want to borrow it.

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:45.291
I can't afford to buy it.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.592
Did you see my tax returns?"

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.094
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:49.995
Democrats were at least
vindicated tonight

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:52.064
in their predictions that
they would win back the House,

00:03:52.064 --> 00:03:53.398
and the story
of how that happened

00:03:53.398 --> 00:03:55.735
is very much about the
two parties' closing messages,

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.303
which could not have been
more different.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:00.472
Democrats' closing message
was primarily about healthcare.

00:04:00.472 --> 00:04:02.742
Trump, on the other hand,
tried scare people

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.844
with racist conspiracy theories
about the migrant caravan

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:07.380
headed toward
the southern border.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.349
The GOP's closing message
was basically this.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:13.453
-We are going to die!

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.520
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.188
-Trump's advisers
pleaded with him

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:18.390
to talk about something else,
like the economy,

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:22.128
and Trump tried but admitted
he found the subject boring.

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:24.296
-And what job numbers
we had today.

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:27.133
Did you hear?
Did you hear?

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.469
Well, we'll go into that.

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.838
They all say,
"Speak with the economy.

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:34.440
Speak about the economy."

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.709
Well, we have
the greatest economy

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.344
in the history of our country.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.445
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.814
But sometimes
it's not as exciting

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.016
to talk about the economy,
right?

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:45.384
-"Did you hear?

00:04:45.384 --> 00:04:48.221
Well, if not, too bad,
'cause I'm not gonna tell you."

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.022
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:53.459
That's the President
saying the economy is boring.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:56.362
Dude, the economy
is your number-one job.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:58.731
It's like getting in an Uber
and hearing your drive say,

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:01.834
"Sometimes it's not exciting
to keep your eyes on the road."

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.269
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.403
Although he's right.

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:06.672
Talking about the economy
isn't as exciting.

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:07.773
You know
who could've told you that?

00:05:07.773 --> 00:05:08.941
Barack Obama.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.609
This dude rescued us
from one of the worst

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:12.077
financial collapses in history,

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:13.846
and every time
he tried to talk about it,

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.180
it was such a snooze fest,

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:17.917
some heckler in the back
would scream, "This is boring!

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.886
Show us your birth certificate!"

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.621
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:23.022
Instead of talking about
the economy,

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.524
Trump tried
a different tactic --

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.325
campaigning with Fox News hosts.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:28.961
Ahead of his final election eve
rally in Missouri last night,

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.831
Trump's campaign announced
that Fox News host Sean Hannity

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.432
would be joining him onstage,

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:36.402
which is weird
since Fox continues to insist

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.470
that it's not an arm
of the Trump administration.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:40.873
So Hannity
issued a correction, tweeting,

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:43.276
"To be clear,
I will not be onstage

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:44.677
campaigning with the President."

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.579
So, there you go, Hannity said
he would not be onstage,

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:50.015
campaigning with the President.
Got it.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:52.318
-Sean Hannity, come on up.
Sean Hannity.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:56.356
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:09.668
Yeah, stay, come on.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:12.538
-By the way, all those people
in the back are fake news.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:16.542
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:20.112
Mr. President, I did
an opening monologue today,

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:22.415
and I had no idea you were
gonna invite me up here.

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:25.517
-Oh, no idea?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.517 --> 00:06:27.620
You ran up on stage
like a contestant

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.822
on "The Price is Right."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:32.024
You had no idea.

00:06:32.024 --> 00:06:33.726
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:36.195
No idea he would call you up.

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:37.396
[ Applause ]

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.299
You just flew all the way
to Missouri on a lark.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.633
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.633 --> 00:06:43.802
Hannity's like a guy who gets
a call from his crush

00:06:43.802 --> 00:06:45.103
and answers on the first ring.

00:06:45.103 --> 00:06:47.373
"Hi! This is Sean.
No, I wasn't just sitting here."

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.407
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.407 --> 00:06:49.742
In fact, Trump was so desperate,

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.277
he brought up a ton
of special guests,

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:54.080
from Sean Hannity
to Rush Limbaugh to Ivanka Trump

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.582
to Fox host Jeanine Pirro
to Kellyanne Conway

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.250
to Sarah Huckabee Sanders.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.485
I mean, look at these creeps.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.153
It's like
the Brotherhood of Mutants.

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:02.454
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.454 --> 00:07:05.024
All they're missing
is Magneto hovering over them.

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:06.559
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:08.160
Now, Trump obviously loomed over

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:10.029
the midterms
and exit polls today.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:12.665
56% said the country
was on the wrong track,

00:07:12.665 --> 00:07:15.000
and 55% disapproved of Trump.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.570
And when Trump tried to campaign
for other Republicans,

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:19.538
the crowds
made it all about him,

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:21.540
as you can tell
from the chants at his rally

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.508
in Missouri last night.

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:24.243
Although, if you listen,

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:26.812
I'm not sure the chants
made a whole lot of sense.

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:29.915
-President Trump got elected
because of the Missourians.

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:33.419
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:36.555
And we're gonna re-elect him!

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:37.556
-Four more years!

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:39.791
-That's right.
-Four more years!

00:07:39.791 --> 00:07:43.061
Four more years!
Four more years!

00:07:43.061 --> 00:07:45.331
-That's right, four more years.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:46.899
They want him to get re-elected,

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:49.401
serve half of his second term,
and that's it.

00:07:49.401 --> 00:07:55.508
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.542
Trump also tried to scare people

00:07:57.542 --> 00:07:59.211
about Democrats'
healthcare plans

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:00.980
by telling them that
the Democrats' push

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.149
for universal healthcare
would destroy Medicare.

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:06.051
Now, healthcare was clearly
a huge issue for voters.

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:09.155
In exit polls, more than 4 in 10
said it was their top priority.

00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:11.290
Trump tried to use that
against Democrats,

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:14.126
but he clearly got some of
his talking points mixed up.

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:16.628
Watch him mess up
and then try on recover

00:08:16.628 --> 00:08:18.664
as if that's
what he meant to say.

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:21.200
-If Democrats gain power
on Tuesday,

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.871
one of their very first projects
will be a socialist takeover

00:08:25.871 --> 00:08:27.172
of American healthcare.

00:08:27.172 --> 00:08:28.307
You know what's happening.

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:31.143
And your taxes are gonna triple,
maybe quadruple.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:34.113
You're not gonna be happy.
I know you well.

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:38.417
The Democrat plan
would obliterate Obamacare.

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:40.519
It will also --
Which is good,

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:43.188
but leave the bad parts behind.

00:08:43.188 --> 00:08:45.224
It will destroy Medicare.

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:48.961
-[ Laughing ]
Nice save, dude.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.629
Whoo!

00:08:50.629 --> 00:08:52.798
He got so confused
by his own B.S.,

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:55.901
he accidentally told his own
supporters to vote Democrat.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.169
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:58.804
"The Democrats' plan is bad

00:08:58.804 --> 00:09:00.873
because it would
obliterate Obamacare --

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:02.140
which is good!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.876
We're against Obamacare,
which is bad!

00:09:04.876 --> 00:09:08.213
So if you want to get rid
of Obamacare, vote...Democrat?

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:10.850
I..."
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.451
So, in the home stretch
of the campaign,

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:15.621
Trump somehow managed to lie
even more than he usually does.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.690
And yet it didn't seem
to bother his supporters.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.225
They either believe
every word he says

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.427
or openly brag
that they don't care.

00:09:21.427 --> 00:09:23.462
One voter at a Trump rally
in Florida over the weekend

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.865
told the "Huffington Post"
that she was not interested

00:09:25.865 --> 00:09:29.201
in whether or how many times
Trump might lie that evening.

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:31.904
"I don't care if he sprouts
a third dick up there."

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:33.405
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.405 --> 00:09:35.341
Wait.
A third?

00:09:35.341 --> 00:09:37.542
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.542 --> 00:09:41.346
Oh, my God. Trump's lying
has gotten so out of control,

00:09:41.346 --> 00:09:46.751
he's been telling his supporters
he already has two penises,

00:09:46.751 --> 00:09:49.054
and they believed him.

00:09:49.054 --> 00:09:52.324
Look, Trump might be happy about
the results in the Senate,

00:09:52.324 --> 00:09:54.193
but the results in the House
are huge.

00:09:54.193 --> 00:09:55.994
Democrats will now be able
to check Trump's power

00:09:55.994 --> 00:09:57.329
and investigate him.

00:09:57.329 --> 00:09:59.497
They're gonna ask
for his tax returns right away.

00:09:59.497 --> 00:10:00.666
And if they get them,

00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:02.634
they're gonna be running
around D.C., saying...

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:04.537
-Did you hear?

00:10:04.537 --> 00:10:05.904
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:10:05.904 --> 00:10:09.241
[ Cheers and applause ]

